    <!-- Memorizing Tips (Tab 4) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle1">🧠 Fast Memorizing Rules</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent1">• Identities 1-2: Square → 3 terms, coefficients 1 · 2 · 1
• Identity 3: Difference of squares → sum × difference
• Identities 4-5: Cube → 4 terms, coefficients 1 · 3 · 3 · 1
• Identities 6-7: Sum/difference of cubes → 2 parentheses product

🔑 The 2nd parenthesis (Id. 6-7): OPPOSITE sign of the 1st</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle2">📐 Pascal's Triangle — Expansion Coefficients</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent2">n=0:        1
n=1:       1  1
n=2:      1  2  1        ← Identities 1, 2
n=3:     1  3  3  1      ← Identities 4, 5
n=4:    1  4  6  4  1
n=5:   1  5 10 10  5  1

→ Each number = sum of two numbers directly above</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle3">⚡ Quick Calculation Tricks</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent3">• 101² = (100+1)² = 10000 + 200 + 1 = 10201
• 99² = (100−1)² = 10000 − 200 + 1 = 9801
• 47×53 = (50−3)(50+3) = 2500 − 9 = 2491
• 98² = (100−2)² = 10000 − 400 + 4 = 9604

💡 Trick: represent numbers in "round number ± delta" form</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle4">🎯 Factoring Polynomials</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent4">• x² + 6x + 9 = (x + 3)²                [Id. 1]
• 4x² − 12x + 9 = (2x − 3)²            [Id. 2]
• 25x² − 16 = (5x+4)(5x−4)            [Id. 3]
• x³ + 8 = (x+2)(x²−2x+4)             [Id. 6]
• 27x³ − 1 = (3x−1)(9x²+3x+1)         [Id. 7]

💡 Always check: "can it be written in A², A³ form?"</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle5">📝 Algebraic Identity Poem</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent5">"The square of a sum
Is first term squared
Add twice their product
Plus second term squared"

"Difference of two squares
Is sum times difference
Remember this well
For high exam score!"</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipTitle6">🔄 Comparing Identity Pairs</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Id_TipContent6">Id. 1 vs 2: Only differs at middle sign → −2AB
Id. 4 vs 5: Alternating signs + − + −
Id. 6 vs 7: The 2nd parenthesis changes AB sign

→ Learn one → easily deduce the other!</sys:String>

